NXR-156|Reproducible IPC models and discriminating ARM witnesses|Verification|IPC verification shall include reproducible reference-state campaigns, exhaustive three-waiter ordering variants, and ARM witnesses that distinguish first-handler catch-up and live-window interruption.|A passing throughput test may miss order, detachment or interrupt-window failures; weak catch-up tests can pass single-tick accounting.|Four seeds cover 600000 operations at three capacities;1296 waiter campaigns cover priorities, ties, expiry and changes; ARM records live-window PC, first elapsed count, preload and extended-time continuity.|Host CTest and actual ARM QEMU campaigns with retained logs.|NXR-154,NXR-155|Fixed-capacity host oracles; optional ARM stress witness hooks default off outside stress presets.|No heap or TCB growth in ordinary firmware; stress-only observer state documented.|tests/ipc_random.cpp,tests/ipc_wait_order.cpp,examples/arm_stress.cpp,ports/arm-mps2/canaries.S,src/kernel.cpp,docs/ipc-stress.rst,docs/arm-canaries.rst|Panel150 test-discrimination findings addressed; host checks are single-CPU models, not SMP or hardware evidence.|tests/ipc_random.cpp,tests/ipc_wait_order.cpp,examples/arm_stress.cpp,ports/arm-mps2/canaries.S,src/kernel.cpp|tests/ipc_random.cpp,tests/ipc_wait_order.cpp,examples/arm_stress.cpp|PartialSourceUnverified
